WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:11.806
Vinnie and Mandy had never seen a square dance before.

2
00:00:11.807 --> 00:00:15.558
Four musicians stood in a corner of the room.

3
00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:18.485
Each one held a different instrument:

4
00:00:18.486 --> 00:00:23.967
a violin, a banjo, a bass fiddle, and a guitar.

5
00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.713
"Everybody, grab your partners!"

6
00:00:26.714 --> 00:00:31.764
shouted the man with the violin, and the band began to play.

7
00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:36.477
"Let's try it," said Vinnie, taking Mandy's hand.

8
00:00:36.478 --> 00:00:41.978
The dancers smiled and laughed as they whirled around the floor.

9
00:00:41.979 --> 00:00:44.568
"This is hard!"

10
00:00:44.569 --> 00:00:48.323
gasped Mandy, trying to do the dance steps.

11
00:00:48.324 --> 00:00:52.558
"Just don't step on my feet!" shouted Vinnie.

12
00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:57.917
Suddenly an old man ran onto the dance floor, shouting.

13
00:00:57.918 --> 00:01:01.123
"There's going to be a shootout!"

14
00:01:01.124 --> 00:01:05.532
The music stopped, and Nellie ran to the children.

15
00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:09.018
"What's a shootout?" Mandy asked.

16
00:01:09.019 --> 00:01:14.056
"It's when two men fight with guns," explained Nellie.

17
00:01:14.057 --> 00:01:20.969
"Young Foster and Wild Bill Hickok are outside!" yelled the old man.

18
00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:24.783
Hearing this, people ran into the street.

19
00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:28.148
Everyone wanted to watch the shootout.

20
00:01:28.149 --> 00:01:32.033
"Who's Wild Bill?" Vinnie asked Nellie.

21
00:01:32.034 --> 00:01:36.363
"He's the famous sheriff from Abilene," she replied.

22
00:01:36.364 --> 00:01:39.538
"And the best shot in the West.

23
00:01:39.539 --> 00:01:42.484
He comes to Dodge City to play cards.

24
00:01:42.485 --> 00:01:44.821
He's good at that too."

25
00:01:44.822 --> 00:01:49.468
"Come on, Mandy," said Vinnie, grabbing her hand.

26
00:01:49.469 --> 00:01:52.322
"Vinnie, I don't like guns!"

27
00:01:52.323 --> 00:01:56.406
cried Mandy, but he pulled her along.

28
00:01:56.407 --> 00:01:59.362
People had gathered along the street.

29
00:01:59.363 --> 00:02:03.418
They watched the two men in the middle of the road.

30
00:02:03.419 --> 00:02:08.855
Standing about fifty meters apart, the men faced each other.

31
00:02:08.856 --> 00:02:13.006
"You're a cheat, Foster," said one of the men.

32
00:02:13.007 --> 00:02:16.269
He had long hair and wore two guns.

33
00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:20.274
"You can't prove it, Wild Bill," shouted the other.

34
00:02:20.275 --> 00:02:24.940
He wiggled his fingers and seemed ready to draw his guns.

35
00:02:24.941 --> 00:02:28.539
"Now gentlemen, you know the rules."

36
00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:33.275
Another man walked over and stood between the gunfighters.

37
00:02:33.276 --> 00:02:38.357
"Hey, Mandy, there's Cookie and Frank!" Vinnie pointed.

38
00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:42.278
The cowboys were watching the shootout too.

39
00:02:42.279 --> 00:02:47.945
"Vinnie! Doesn't this remind you of the photo?" asked Mandy.

40
00:02:47.946 --> 00:02:53.276
She pulled the photo out of her pocket, and it was glowing blue.

41
00:02:53.277 --> 00:02:58.748
She saw that the two men in the street were the same as in the photo.

42
00:02:58.749 --> 00:03:03.947
"Calm down, Wild Bill," said a woman in a red dress.

43
00:03:03.948 --> 00:03:08.471
She came out of the saloon holding some coins in her hand.

44
00:03:08.472 --> 00:03:12.112
"Foster is just a kid—"

45
00:03:12.113 --> 00:03:18.142
Suddenly, she tripped and the coins flew high into the air.

46
00:03:18.143 --> 00:03:25.143
Wild Bill drew his guns as fast as lightning and shot the five coins one after the other.

47
00:03:25.144 --> 00:03:27.745
The coins never hit the ground.

48
00:03:27.746 --> 00:03:30.237
The crowd cheered.

49
00:03:30.238 --> 00:03:32.336
"Vinnie! This is it!"

50
00:03:32.337 --> 00:03:38.088
Mandy said excitedly as the photo glowed red.

51
00:03:38.089 --> 00:03:45.236
The children shut their eyes and fell down the dark tunnel.

52
00:03:45.237 --> 00:03:48.065
They landed back in the attic.

53
00:03:48.066 --> 00:03:57.066
"We didn't get to see the shootout," said Vinnie, disappointed.
